  "name": "COMPLEMENT 4 (C4 )",
  "code": "2002",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Complement is a group of 20 immunologically distinct proteins present in blood and tissues. They are synthesized in liver&nbsp;and are present in serum as functionally inactive molecules. C4 complement is a a-glycoprotein of 3 sub units. C4 C is a&nbsp;constituent of C3 convertase and C5 convertase. Decreased levels are found in hereditary angioneuroticodema, immune&nbsp;complex disease and congential dificiencies. The reagent is linear up to 80 mg/dl. Lower detection limit is 3 mg/dl.&nbsp;</p>",
